now have a combined annual revenue run

295
00:10:16,537 --> 00:10:19,524
rate of more than ten billion dollars.

296
00:10:19,524 --> 00:10:21,908
And Microsoft expects to spend more than

297
00:10:21,908 --> 00:10:24,529
fifty billion dollars in its next quarter

298
00:10:24,529 --> 00:10:25,606
alone.

299
00:10:25,850 --> 00:10:28,481
So here is the one number to

300
00:10:28,481 --> 00:10:29,220
watch.

301
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:30,550
Not the spending.

302
00:10:30,550 --> 00:10:32,100
The backlog.

303
00:10:32,100 --> 00:10:34,279
As long as customers keep signing

304
00:10:34,279 --> 00:10:36,700
contracts faster than the companies can

305
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:37,160
build,

306
00:10:37,160 --> 00:10:38,950
the bet is paying off.

307
00:10:38,950 --> 00:10:41,377
If the backlog stops growing while the

308
00:10:41,377 --> 00:10:42,809
spending keeps rising,

309
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:45,721
the data centers become very expensive

310
00:10:45,721 --> 00:10:47,049
empty rooms.

311
00:10:47,284 --> 00:10:49,391
So how does Big Tech really make

312
00:10:49,391 --> 00:10:51,044
money from AI?

313
00:10:51,224 --> 00:10:53,059
By renting the machines,

314
00:10:53,059 --> 00:10:54,661
by selling better ads,

315
00:10:54,661 --> 00:10:57,584
and by locking in customers for years.

316
00:10:57,604 --> 00:11:00,364
The chatbot is the shop window.

317
00:11:00,454 --> 00:11:02,684
The real business is behind it,

318
00:11:02,684 --> 00:11:04,239
in the data centers,

319
00:11:04,239 --> 00:11:05,568
in the ad auctions,

320
00:11:05,568 --> 00:11:07,370
and in contracts that will pay out

321
00:11:07,370 --> 00:11:10,448
long after the next model is released.

322
00:11:10,684 --> 00:11:13,182
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

323
00:11:13,182 --> 00:11:16,161
we follow the money behind another hidden

324
00:11:16,161 --> 00:11:18,594
link of the world economy.

325
00:11:18,704 --> 00:11:21,138
This is The Hidden Economics.
